TWCA SSL Certification Authority -- the intermediate www.parkinginfo.ntpc.gov.tw
does not send, shipped so New Taipei's chain can be built.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
  Measured 2026-09-17 from inside the collector image (python 3.13.15,
  OpenSSL 3.5.7, certifi 2026.07.22): www.parkinginfo.ntpc.gov.tw sends
  exactly ONE certificate -- its leaf -- and no intermediate. Verification
  therefore fails with "unable to get local issuer certificate". Clearing
  ssl.VERIFY_X509_STRICT does NOT help; the issuer is genuinely absent.
  This file supplies it.

  It adds NO NEW TRUST ANCHOR. This certificate is itself issued by
  "TWCA CYBER Root CA", which certifi 2026.07.22 already ships as a trusted
  root. Supplying it only lets OpenSSL complete a path to a root the
  collector already trusted; it is loaded IN ADDITION TO certifi's bundle
  (see sources/http.py, TlsPolicy.extra_ca_file), never instead of it, and
  New Taipei keeps full strict verification -- hostname checking on,
  CERT_REQUIRED, VERIFY_X509_STRICT on.

PROVENANCE
  Source        http://sslserver.twca.com.tw/cacert/Cyber_SSL_2023.crt
                (the CA Issuers URI in the New Taipei leaf's own Authority
                Information Access extension)
  Fetched       2026-09-17, from inside the collector image; 1752 bytes DER,
                converted to PEM with ssl.DER_cert_to_PEM_cert
  Subject       C=TW, O=TAIWAN-CA, OU=SSL Sub-CA,
                CN=TWCA SSL Certification Authority
  Issuer        C=TW, O=TAIWAN-CA, OU=Root CA, CN=TWCA CYBER Root CA
  Serial        400134B04F0000000000000003E324AC
  SHA-256       01:AF:23:24:D0:98:09:8F:5E:0C:DF:6F:AA:BA:DA:43:
                0B:21:CC:E7:77:F4:7E:AC:B2:62:48:B2:FD:A3:E5:31
  Not before    Feb 23 07:22:24 2023 GMT
  Not after     Feb 23 15:59:59 2033 GMT
  Key usage     critical: Certificate Sign, CRL Sign
  Basic constr. critical: CA:TRUE, pathlen:0

CHAIN PROOF (openssl 3.5.7, in-container, 2026-09-17; certifi's bundle plus
this one file, ordinary verification, no relaxations)

    $ openssl verify -CAfile $(python -c 'import certifi;print(certifi.where())') \
          -untrusted twca-ssl-ca-2023.pem -show_chain leaf.pem
    leaf.pem: OK
    Chain:
    depth=0: C=TW, L=New Taipei, O=..., CN=www.parkinginfo.ntpc.gov.tw (untrusted)
    depth=1: C=TW, O=TAIWAN-CA, OU=SSL Sub-CA, CN=TWCA SSL Certification Authority (untrusted)
    depth=2: C=TW, O=TAIWAN-CA, OU=Root CA, CN=TWCA CYBER Root CA

  Without this file the same command fails: "error 20 at 0 depth lookup:
  unable to get local issuer certificate". The same chain also verifies with
  OpenSSL's own -x509_strict, which is why New Taipei does not need, and does
  not get, the flag relaxation Kaohsiung and Hsinchu use.

WHEN IT EXPIRES OR STOPS MATCHING
  tests/test_sources_tls.py asserts this file parses and is inside its
  validity window, so it fails the suite before it fails a fetch. If TWCA
  rotates the intermediate, New Taipei's fetch raises requests.exceptions.
  SSLError and the source reads FAILED on its health line. It never degrades
  to unverified -- nothing in this codebase can turn verification off.

